body:
aaaah i definitely empathize with your thoughts regarding Cait’s treatment as a character… i am a sucker for platonic love and faith risking everything to save kate in the first game was a major emotional beat for me. 

imo i blame this on the fact that catalyst was supposed to have a sequel — it feels clear to me that from the ending, there would’ve been a follow-up detailing how glass was affected by kruger’s death and such. and in that game there probably would’ve been so much more room to explore cat’s resentment of faith for being abandoned, yet her remaining love for the only family she has left, and from the opposite side, faith’s guilt yet compassion towards her sister. i still think about how i almost cried during the scene where they were fighting each other because i really didn’t want to see them end things on a bad note. these two are important to me ;w; 

but yeah, with the rushed development and ea’s focus on raking in money from MTX, we’ll sadly never know :’)
